---
import PolicyPage from "@/components/layout/PolicyPage.astro";
import { updateManifest } from "@/data/policies";
import { site } from "@/data/site";
---

<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Muelle has no accounts, analytics or telemetry. Its optional network request checks for updates."
  updated="November 16, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Muelle has no accounts, no analytics and no telemetry. It does not collect personal data and never sends anything
    to the Muelle project. Its only automatic request is the one below, and it can be turned off in Settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Update check</h2>
  <p>
    When you open Settings, and once a day, Muelle asks GitHub
    whether a newer version exists by downloading{" "}
    <code>{updateManifest}</code>. Nothing about you or your computer is sent with it; GitHub, like any website, sees
    your IP address and handles it under the{" "}
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub privacy statement</a>.
    When there is one, Settings opens to tell you. Its signed installer is downloaded from the same GitHub releases
    page and installed only when you choose to.
  </p>
  <p>To turn it off: Settings → System → <b>Check for updates automatically</b>. You can still check by hand.</p>

  <h2>What stays on your computer</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>%APPDATA%\Muelle\config.json</code>: your settings and the apps you pinned.</li>
    <li><code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Muelle</code>: a cache of app icons and names, so the dock starts fast.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To show what is on screen (open windows, their icons, network and volume status, and whether an app is using the
    microphone or camera, for the menu bar), Muelle asks Windows itself; none of it leaves your computer. Uninstalling removes the cache, and optionally your settings.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Vercel and uses no cookies, analytics or trackers. Vercel may keep standard server logs (such
    as IP addresses) under the{" "}
    <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel privacy policy</a>.
    Downloads come from <a href={site.releases} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Releases</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={site.issues} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
